From 708163476d0e8a9b78e3203458b886d76ecfe40e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 08:42:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] spec: ingest turboquant MTP-boost wave + effective-KV bench
 reporting

Ten commits from llama-cpp-turboquant d14e36827..bd1bf025f (feature/turboquant-kv-cache),
applied as one ingest wave; the raw 10-commit stack with original authorship is kept on
branch tq-ingest-raw-backup. Content: chained MTP drafting with adaptive depth
(COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_DRAFT_MTP_ADAPTIVE, speculative-adaptive.h, qwen35 chain path),
MTP chain batching/capability hardening, stale MTP draft-KV trims (after position rewind,
before deferred flush, before chain decode, at trim sites incl. parallel deferred-row
pollution), deferred-row prefill accounting, failed-rewind surfacing, llama-bench
effective-KV-type reporting, DSV4 unreportable-type comment fix, plus tests
(test-speculative-adaptive, arg-parser rows).

Three conflicts resolved by hand, recorded in the lane-161 DECISIONS file:
llama-context.cpp include block (their unconditional kv-cache include list subsumes our
GGML_ARIFI_KV_MEANCENTER-guarded subset), and two speculative.cpp regions where our
add_config_if_enabled refactor replaces their per-type bool chain - the adaptive type
was folded into our shape as one add_config_if_enabled row.

Taken-from: llama-cpp-turboquant@bd1bf025f (524531e57, f9e04f5d7, 4be91d62b, 5b105dfb7, 4c4131bf8, b20e97012, 7544b18cf, 275963f50, cd638bc13, e82fe159b)
Origin: git am --3way of the range; 3 hand-resolved conflicts folded to our refactored shapes
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED (their mtp-boost numbers are theirs; no arm run on this rig yet)
